WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.140
Good Morning John.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:04.470
So it's a little shocking to me and like a
lot of other people that a fourteen year old

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.220
kid in a NASA shirt brought a clock that he
built to school to show his engineering teacher

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.390
and was arrested and taken to a juvenile detention
center.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:16.429
But then on the other hand, it's not shocking
because Ahmed Mohamed's name is Ahmed Mohamed

00:00:16.429 --> 00:00:18.000
and he is Muslim.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.099
And many people in America are afraid of Muslims.

00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:24.400
Now I'm not going to make a video here about
how the vast vast vast majority of Muslims,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.660
just like any other broad diverse group of
people, are good people.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.449
Two reasons for that: first, finding these
statistics on the internet that make this

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.600
very clear is pretty easy.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.829
Second, making a video defending Muslims would
ignore the actual problem which is the bias

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:46.079
and the fear mongering that creates suspicion
and hatred and those things are our problems.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:51.000
And our problems we can deal with so much
more easily than trying to deal with other

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.340
people's problems, especially when those problems
are imagined.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:57.449
Now of course, it's not super comfortable
to recognize your own problems and it doesn't

00:00:57.449 --> 00:01:01.100
make you feel all good which is why this video
is not gonna go super viral.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.100
But since it is the actual problem, and also
one that we can deal with conceivably since

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.909
we are the ones with the problem, that's what
I want to make the video about.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:15.299
So why do so many Americans, including, I'll
be honest sometimes myself, fall into this

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:16.299
fear trap?

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:19.490
First, because it's just impossible to know
everything about everyone, and though Muslims

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:24.130
have been in America since America existed,
they are a significant minority, less than

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.130
1%.

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:27.960
So most Americans simply don't know much about
Muslims or the Islamic faith.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:32.380
But we do hear about Muslims fairly regularly
on the news, and we hear about the scariest

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:33.380
Muslims in the world.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:36.780
So if you're expected to have an idea of what
Muslim people are like and this is the only

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.790
input you're getting, you're gonna have a
really messed up idea.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.030
It's an easy mistake for a brain to make,
but it is a huge mistake, because we know

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.030
nothing!

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:48.409
An example: What percentage of Muslims would
you say live in the Middle East?

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:50.310
80%? 85%?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.860
That's what I would've said before starting
to research this video.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.670
How about 20%? 60% of Muslims live in Asia.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.120
The single country with the largest Muslim
population?

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.120
Indonesia.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.759
If we are ignorant of such a basic fact, how
could we consider ourselves qualified to make

00:02:04.759 --> 00:02:08.110
sweeping generalizations about a broad and
diverse group of people?

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:12.200
Once these negative ideas are set up in our
brain, they can be easily reinforced in people

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.480
who are motivated by fear and outrage.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.580
Those people watch other people on TV who
professionally cultivate outrage and fear

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.560
because it's good for ratings, and that fear
then prevents conversations and causes the

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.569
majority to isolate Muslims from their broader
communities by doing thing like, for example,

00:02:27.569 --> 00:02:29.560
arresting a kid for bringing a clock to class.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:34.790
So the fear builds on itself until what was
once ignorance and became fear eventually

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.790
becomes hatred.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.930
And once you hate someone, they know it.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.010
Muslims in America are certainly not ignorant
of the hatred and the discrimination, but

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.280
Muslims in other countries aren't ignorant
of the more extreme American views, either.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.550
In fact, I'm willing to bet that in the same
way that we are mostly just about scary Muslims

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:54.260
on American news, in other countries they
hear mostly about the scariest versions of

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.260
Americans.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.040
And if people in other countries are gonna
put us in a little box, which they are bound

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:00.830
to do because no one can know everything about
everyone, what little box do we want to get

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.830
put into?

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.990
Do we want to be in the "hates Muslims" box,
or do we want to be in the "values religious

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.629
freedom and provides opportunities for people
who seek it" box.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:10.709
I think we should fight that fear.

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:15.040
I think we can fight that fear and the only
way to do it, the only place to do it is up

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.040
here.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.319
It's right in here.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:18.879
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

